  "scopeFindings": [
    "The NHGRI open-reading-frame definition is a stretch without a stop in a frame; the lesson's start-to-stop convention is not the sole annotation definition.",
    "A three-base deletion preserves downstream frame but does not guarantee one clean codon deletion or protein function.",
    "Crick's primary article argues for three or a multiple of three and notes partial function; the schematic explanation is qualified accordingly.",
    "The NCBI mitochondrial table and its older mechanistic comment are distinct; later primary experiments on mtRF1/mtRF1L are not replaced by an unqualified frameshift-only mechanism.",
    "ClinVar aggregate expert-panel classifications were read at the VCV level, not inferred from the first condition-specific RCV child.",
    "Le's reported objective response denominator is 86 (46 responses); the detailed mutant-peptide experiment is from one responding person.",
    "A single ClinVar example is not a frequency survey of inherited BRCA variant classes.",
    "Sakai's named model evidence does not support a universal pooled reversion prevalence, guaranteed clinical non-response or a negative-reversion rechallenge rule."
  ],
